/-!
# Even-weight dimension lower bound for M_k(Γ₁(M))

Theorem statement: `ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card_of_even`
(`9935fe93-ca4a-50ab-99f5-609a2e925be9`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `174702df-0d5d-58f7-98fb-fcc34a6e0712`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $M$ be a positive integer with $M \ge 5$, and let $k$ be a natural number with $3 \le k$ and $k$
even. The assertion is that there exist a natural number $d$ and a family $f : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to
\mathrm{ModularForm}\,(\Gamma_1(M))\,k$ of modular forms of weight $k$ (the integer cast of $k$) for
the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(M) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, linearly independent over
$\mathbb{C}$, such that
$$(k-1)\,\big[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}) : \Gamma_1(M)\,\sqcup\,\langle -1\rangle\big] \;+\;
6\,\#\big(\Gamma_1(M)\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\langle T, -1\rangle\big) \;\le\; 12\,d
.$$
Here the first index is the index, as a natural number, of the subgroup of
$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ generated by $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with $-1$ (the join of $\Gamma_1(M)$
with the subgroup of integer powers of $-1$); $k-1$ is truncated subtraction of naturals, harmless
since $k \ge 3$; and the second term counts the double cosets of $\Gamma_1(M)$ and of the subgroup
generated by the translation matrix $T$ and $-1$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, as the cardinality
of the corresponding double coset quotient. Thus $\dim_{\mathbb{C}} M_k(\Gamma_1(M)) \ge d$ is
bounded below by one twelfth of the displayed expression.

This is the even-weight case of the classical lower bound on the dimension of the space of
weight-$k$ modular forms on $\Gamma_1(M)$, the right-hand side of the classical dimension formula
for $M \ge 5$ (no elliptic points, all cusps regular) being written in terms of the index of
$\pm\Gamma_1(M)$ and the number of cusps presented as a double coset count. It is combined with the
odd-weight case in
[`ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card`]
(thm.html#ModularForm.exists_linearIndependent_gamma1_dimFormula_le_card),
which supplies the supply of forms needed later in the argument.

